From: openEuler RISC-V package contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] resolver: bound all DNS compression jumps without recursion

A compression self-pointer or cycle repeats the recursive decoder arguments.
Iterate over pointer jumps with one per-name budget derived from message size.
Keep the first pointer's outer compressed length while appending labels to
the original bounded output buffer. Valid acyclic compression is preserved;
cycles fail with the existing zero/error convention without recursive stack growth.

Downstream-only source-risk repair; no upstream write or CVE claim.
Deterministic parser regression and original-source instrumentation control
run only in target CI, never during local tooling validation.

--- a/src/resolver.c
+++ b/src/resolver.c
@@ -86 +86,2 @@
-    unsigned rc;
+    unsigned consumed = 0;
+    size_t hops_left = buf_len;
@@ -110,12 +111,8 @@
-            if (name != NULL && name_len >= name_max && name_max > 0) {
-                /* We have filled the name buffer. Don't pass it recursively. */
-                name[name_max - 1] = '\0';
-                name = NULL;
-                name_max = 0;
-            }
-            rc = message_name_get(buf, buf_len, pointer,
-                                  name != NULL ? &name[name_len] : NULL,
-                                  name_max > name_len ? name_max - name_len : 0);
-            if (rc == 0) return 0;
-            /* Pointer is always the last. */
-            break;
+            /* All jumps share one finite budget, including jumps after labels.
+             * Iterate rather than grow the stack on an attacker-controlled chain.
+             * A valid acyclic chain cannot visit more offsets than buf_len.
+             */
+            if (hops_left == 0) return 0;
+            --hops_left;
+            if (consumed == 0) consumed = i - buf_offset;
+            i = pointer;
@@ -144 +141 @@
-    return i - buf_offset;
+    return consumed != 0 ? consumed : i - buf_offset;
